This submodule is a toolbox, not part of aion_chip's FuseSoC library.

aion_chip/fusesoc.conf declares `[library.aion] location = .`, which walks the
whole project. Without this marker FuseSoC also picks up aion_flow/tech/tech.core,
which declares the same VLNV as aion_chip/tech/tech.core -- epfl:aion:tech:1.0.0 --
but points at the *timing* cell models. The submodule wins the tie by walk order,
so every gate-level simulation silently elaborates with the wrong models:

    WARNING: Replacing epfl:aion:tech:1.0.0 in <aion_chip>/tech
             with the version found in <aion_chip>/aion_flow/tech

Verilator then gets the primitive/table UDPs instead of the zero-delay
behavioural replacements and the run hangs at 0 ns.

FuseSoC skips any directory tree containing a file with this name
(fusesoc/coremanager.py: find_cores -> `ignore_tree = "FUSESOC_IGNORE" in files`).
aion_flow's own cores are still usable from inside aion_flow.
